WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.089 --> 00:00:04.170
Good morning Hank, it's Monday, February 14th,
2011. I recently saw a YouTuber I like a lot

00:00:04.170 --> 00:00:07.530
named 'idointernet' play a game called 'Chubby
Bunny'.

00:00:07.530 --> 00:00:10.820
Hank, the rules are you just eat marshmallows
and say 'Chubby Bunny', it's pretty easy,

00:00:10.820 --> 00:00:17.300
watch me. (puts one marshmallow in mouth)
Chubby bunny... chubby bunny... This is almost

00:00:17.300 --> 00:00:24.619
too easy. Chubby bunny... chubby bunny...(laughs)
This just got much harder... chubby bunny...

00:00:24.619 --> 00:00:32.500
this one is going to be quite a challenge
Hank... chubby... Wait a second. Did I say

00:00:32.500 --> 00:00:37.020
it's February 14th, 2011? Is this Valentine's
Day?

00:00:37.020 --> 00:00:42.450
(without marshmallows) It's Valentine's Day,
isn't it, Hank? ...CRAP!

00:00:42.450 --> 00:00:45.910
OK Hank I have to go to the mall, walk with
me. OK, so three things I hate about Valentine's

00:00:45.910 --> 00:00:49.960
Day. Number one: all gift giving is economically
inefficient, but Valentine's Day is the worst,

00:00:49.960 --> 00:00:55.020
because you almost always give people stuff
they wouldn't choose to own themselves, like

00:00:55.020 --> 00:01:00.190
candy hearts or the necklace that my wife
colloquially refers to as 'Boobs and Butt'.

00:01:00.190 --> 00:01:04.159
Actually, I should probably just get her that
necklace. Instead, I am buying her shampoo.

00:01:04.159 --> 00:01:07.569
Good Lord, Hank, I've purchased cars that
cost less than that shampoo.

00:01:07.569 --> 00:01:12.119
Secondly, Valentine's Day is perhaps the most
potent symbol of our weird obsession with

00:01:12.119 --> 00:01:15.920
romantic love. Like why isn't 'Best Friends
Day' the biggest shopping day of the year?

00:01:15.920 --> 00:01:20.490
Because for some reason, we think you can
only have loving, sustained relationships

00:01:20.490 --> 00:01:22.649
with someone who you also sleep with.

00:01:22.649 --> 00:01:25.920
If you spend your life singularly obsessed
with romantic love, you're gonna miss out

00:01:25.920 --> 00:01:30.020
on a lot of what's fun about being a person,
...also you're gonna have to spend a lot of

00:01:30.020 --> 00:01:31.139
money on diamonds.

00:01:31.139 --> 00:01:36.369
Lastly, I like holidays that celebrate service
or sacrifice, historical figures who embodied

00:01:36.369 --> 00:01:40.611
our values. But I don't really see a point
of a holiday that celebrates romantic love,

00:01:40.611 --> 00:01:45.630
I mean if you need to be reminded to like
your romantic partner, you're doing it wrong.

00:01:45.630 --> 00:01:49.539
Hank, so far as I can tell the only good thing
about Valentine's Day is that gift-giving,

00:01:49.539 --> 00:01:53.931
while it is economically inefficient, is also
kind of an act of empathy. Right? You have

00:01:53.931 --> 00:01:57.709
to imagine what it's like to be someone else,
imagine what they would want, and then get

00:01:57.709 --> 00:01:58.709
it for them.

00:01:58.709 --> 00:02:01.299
But if I'm really being empathetic, Hank,
I'll recognize that what the Yeti wants most

00:02:01.299 --> 00:02:05.340
of all for Valentine's Day is not hastily
purchased toiletries but for me to have this

00:02:05.340 --> 00:02:09.000
video finished and uploaded by the time she
gets home from work. So I'm going to get on

00:02:09.000 --> 00:02:10.000
that.

00:02:10.000 --> 00:02:13.239
Hank, by the way, great job with Your Pants!
...is a sentence I never thought I'd say.

00:02:13.239 --> 00:02:14.870
I'll see you on Wednesday.

00:02:14.870 --> 00:02:19.150
P.S. Hank Green, noted American vlogbrother,
just did a very funny Valentine's Day Truth

00:02:19.150 --> 00:02:26.049
or Fail. Click anywhere on the screen to go
to that! Click now; you're not missing anything.

00:02:26.049 --> 00:02:26.750
Best wishes.

